Shilpa Shetty is set to return as a host with a new reality show titled Pyaar Ka Pressure Cooker. The relationship-based reality series will air on Colors and stream on JioHotstar. The show will bring couples under one roof as they confront relationship issues, discuss their future together and seek clarity on their equations.The format will explore subjects such as situationships, commitment issues and uncertainty about taking relationships forward. It will also involve the parents of the participating couples, who will share their perspectives through segments titled 'Jodo Ya Todo' and 'Clarity Ki Seeti'. The show is expected to take over the time slot currently occupied by Bigg Boss.Speaking about the concept and her association with the show, Shilpa said, “Relationships today come with a whole new vocabulary, from situationships and breadcrumbing to benching, and somewhere along the way, clarity got lost.”She further explained what interested her about the format, adding, “What excites me about 'Pyaar Ka Pressure Cooker' is its fresh take on the reality format... It's relatable for couples, and just as much for the parents watching.”&nbsp;
View this post on Instagram
&nbsp;
A post shared by Shilpa Shetty Kundra (@theshilpashetty)
Pyaar Ka Pressure Cooker marks Shilpa's second hosting assignment this year after Maa Hai Na. The actor has also been associated with several television reality shows as a judge, including Super Dancer and Jhalak Dikhhla Jaa.With its focus on relationship dynamics and family involvement, the upcoming show will bring couples and their parents into conversations about commitment, compatibility and the decisions that shape their relationships. Further details about its premiere date and participating couples are awaited.Also Read: Shilpa Shetty, Arjun Kapoor, and more discuss happiness at India’s FIRST World Happpiness Summit: “Gratitude is something that you have to practice”

The trailer of Nanhey Dil, starring Suniel Shetty, has been released, offering a glimpse into a story centred on childhood, equality and equal opportunities. Written and directed by Swarup Raj Medara, the film highlights how talent and aspirations should not be limited by social or economic backgrounds. Following its screening at international film festivals, the film is now gearing up for a theatrical release on November 20, 2026.Suniel Shetty plays the principal of a prestigious school who recognises the potential of Raghu, a young boy whose father works as a dhobi. Believing that a child's abilities should not be judged by their family background, the principal gives Raghu an opportunity to study alongside children from privileged families. Through this story, the film explores the importance of providing every child with equal opportunities and the freedom to pursue their dreams.Talking about what attracted him to the project, Suniel Shetty said, "Nanhey Dil is a film about children, about giving equal opportunities to everybody and how important it is for us to make sure everybody is comfortable. It has a beautiful message and could definitely be an eye-opener for modern-day parents. I think this generation believes in equality, and that you have to live your dream and not live the dream of your parents. I'd want my children to live their dream, not mine. I think today's parents are all about honesty, and taking care of their parents and children. So hats off to this generation. I took this film on because it was a simple story to tell and I am glad that such stories are being heard and are finding global platforms."&nbsp;
View this post on Instagram
&nbsp;
A post shared by Swarupraj medara (@swarupraj_medara)
Shot over 37 days, the film is titled Fly High Little Hearts for international audiences. It has been screened at international platforms, including the Toronto International Film Festival, as it continues its journey beyond Indian cinema. Its subject of empathy, inclusion and equal opportunities forms the central theme of the narrative.Presented by Srinathji's Hospitality and Ninefold Pictures, Nanhey Dil is a Navaras Entertainment production. The film is produced by Sowmay Jain, Shriya Torne, Dhruva Karunakar and Aishwarya Yadav, with Saiwyn Quadras serving as the creative producer and screenplay writer.Also Read : EXCLUSIVE: Suniel Shetty reveals Awara Paagal Deewana sequel will go on floors early next year: “It’s happening for sure”; also lists Sabse Bada Rupaiya as another upcoming film

Actor-producer Rana Daggubati unveiled the first asset of Scary Picture, an upcoming horror film featuring Kangana Ranaut in the lead role. On Friday, November 13, Rana shared the first glimpse of the project on Instagram. The reveal coincided with Friday the 13th, a date often associated with horror, mystery and superstition, adding to the theme of the announcement.The film is produced by veteran producer Suresh Babu under the banner of Suresh Productions, which has been associated with mainstream Telugu cinema and family entertainers for several decades. With Scary Picture, the production house ventures into the horror genre, marking a shift towards a different kind of storytelling.&nbsp;
View this post on Instagram
&nbsp;
A post shared by Suresh Productions (@sureshproductions)
Speaking about the film and his plans for the genre, Rana Daggubati said, “What we want, starting with Scary Picture, is to create a consistent stream of production support and release opportunities for filmmakers who love this genre. India is diverse in every genre, and horror is no different. Every region has its own fears, its own stories and its own ways of telling them. We’re open to every subgenre: psychological, creature, horror-comedy, social horror, or whatever new narratives filmmakers bring to us.”Directed by Telugu filmmaker Ravi Babu, Scary Picture marks his directorial debut in Hindi cinema. Ravi Babu has previously explored the horror genre through Telugu films such as Anasuya and Avunu. The upcoming film brings him together with Kangana Ranaut for a narrative that aims to explore a different space within the genre.Apart from the film itself, the project also reflects Rana Daggubati's plans to develop a dedicated platform for horror filmmaking in India. Through Suresh Productions and Spirit Media, he aims to provide filmmakers working in the genre with regular production support and opportunities to bring their projects to theatres.With Suresh Babu backing the project and Kangana Ranaut leading the cast, Scary Picture marks a new venture for the production banner as it explores horror storytelling.Also Read : Subhash Ghai brings Aamir Khan, Hema Malini, Rana Daggubati and Imtiaz Ali together for Celebrate Cinema Festival 2026

Netflix is set to release O Saathi Re, a romantic drama series created, written and showrun by Imtiaz Ali, on December 4, 2026. Directed by Arif Ali, the Window Seat Films production features Aditi Rao Hydari, Avinash Tiwary and Arjun Rampal in lead roles. The series explores the complexities of love, emotional imbalances in relationships and the challenges faced by a couple navigating separation.Produced by Imtiaz Ali, Mohit Choudhary and Shibasish Sarkar, O Saathi Re follows layered characters as they navigate the different dimensions of love and relationships. From understanding individual identities and personal desires to examining power dynamics and the difficult process of letting go, the series looks at romance beyond conventional notions of togetherness. At its centre is a relationship in which affection exists, but the balance of love is not necessarily equal.Speaking about the series, Imtiaz Ali said, “O Saathi Re is a modern romantic show with a vintage heart. Sometimes, love surprises you by showing itself in the most unexpected corners. This is the story of the growth of affection in a divorcing couple. Affection has a throbbing heart, love is beautiful, but a relationship can be unequal. To be a matched couple can often be a burden. In O Saathi Re, we see that while love is yearning, dreaming, and getting together, it can also be the process of letting go. The characters are multi-layered and lifelike, which is why we went for the highest grade of actors. The cast, headlined by Aditi Rao Hydari, Avinash Tiwary, and Arjun Rampal, negotiates steep curves and sensitive moments in the captainship of Arif Ali, the director. We’ve had a wonderful run of partnership with Netflix with the experiences of She and Amar Singh Chamkila. We couldn’t have conceived this series without them. We present O Saathi Re with love and hope people like it.”&nbsp;
